From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:50:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Quick Options detail headers keep their glyph in light
 mode

A Quick Options detail marks its header glyph .active while its toggle is
on. Upstream's rule paints an active glyph in the accent foreground, white,
on an accent disc; Luma's detail header draws no disc, so in light mode the
glyph of every detail whose toggle was on (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, Tiling and the
rest) was white on the white detail and vanished. The header glyph is now
the detail's ink whether the toggle is on or off, in both variant sheets.

The light detail's subtitle ink (header subtitle and device subtitles) moves
from #767b81 to #6b7076, from 4.27:1 to 5.0:1 on the white detail.
---
 data/theme/gnome-shell-dark.css  | 10 +++++++++-
 data/theme/gnome-shell-light.css | 14 +++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/theme/gnome-shell-dark.css b/data/theme/gnome-shell-dark.css
index 5139aad..31dbc64 100644
--- a/data/theme/gnome-shell-dark.css
+++ b/data/theme/gnome-shell-dark.css
@@ -4189,7 +4189,15 @@ StScrollBar {
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .header .icon {
     icon-size: 18px;
     padding: 0;
-    background-color: transparent; }
+    background-color: transparent;
+    color: #e9ebec; }
+  /* The detail header's icon is a plain glyph in the detail's ink whether
+   * the toggle is on or off: upstream's .active rule paints it in the accent
+   * foreground (white) for an accent disc Luma does not draw, which left it
+   * white on the light detail. */
+  .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .header .icon.active {
+    background-color: transparent;
+    color: #e9ebec; }
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .header .title {
     font-size: 13px;
     font-weight: 700; }
diff --git a/data/theme/gnome-shell-light.css b/data/theme/gnome-shell-light.css
index e4dc950..158e2ae 100644
--- a/data/theme/gnome-shell-light.css
+++ b/data/theme/gnome-shell-light.css
@@ -4377,13 +4377,21 @@ StScrollBar {
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .header .icon {
     icon-size: 18px;
     padding: 0;
-    background-color: transparent; }
+    background-color: transparent;
+    color: #30343a; }
+  /* The detail header's icon is a plain glyph in the detail's ink whether
+   * the toggle is on or off: upstream's .active rule paints it in the accent
+   * foreground (white) for an accent disc Luma does not draw, which left it
+   * white on the light detail. */
+  .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .header .icon.active {
+    background-color: transparent;
+    color: #30343a; }
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .header .title {
     font-size: 13px;
     font-weight: 700; }
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .header .subtitle {
     font-size: 11px;
-    color: #767b81; }
+    color: #6b7076; }
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .popup-menu-item {
     min-height: 0;
     padding: 10px;
@@ -4395,7 +4403,7 @@ StScrollBar {
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .nm-network-item .wireless-secure-icon {
     width: 7px; }
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .device-subtitle {
-    color: #767b81; }
+    color: #6b7076; }
   .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .keyboard-brightness-level {
     spacing: 6px; }
     .quick-toggle-menu.luma-quick-detail .keyboard-brightness-level .button {
-- 
